  "boundaries": [
    "This is the explicit read-only primary-data inspection prerequisite; no repair command, automatic startup scan, replacement fetch, index rebuild, quarantine or repair publication is implemented.",
    "Tests use isolated finite local fixtures and no live peers/production data/remote host. Original startup remains intentionally lightweight; draft before/after controls are development regressions, not original-repository findings.",
    "The returned inspection retains exclusive cooperative inode ownership. Immutability checks cover contents, directory entries and modification times; filesystem read access times are not covered.",
    "Caller source limits bound specified row/artifact/decode work, not RSS. Existing format-bounded catalog/manifest/bundle metadata loads precede those allowances. Captured raw lengths constrain inspection reads after preflight.",
    "Logical commitment verification and catalog extrema do not establish consensus truth or complete-block coverage. Derived indexes and redundant manifest-bound hints are not exhaustively verified; incomplete recovery is preserved and blocks source verdicts.",
    "Ordinary ingestion and query limits, persisted formats, write barriers and toolchain/dependencies are unchanged. No throughput improvement or benchmark claim is made.",
    "Two draft code gaps (empty raw sources and bundled ID/kind comparison) and an invalid unbound-fixture assumption were resolved before source freeze. Present empty paged/canonical artifacts remain structurally checked.",
    "Offline repair, networking/query policy, integrated acceptance and later live/staging validation remain open."
  ]
